        "type": "Module",
        "name": "preamplifier",
        "description": "NE5532 dual low-noise operational amplifier used as the low-level preamplifier domain. This module accepts the external audio input, provides voltage amplification, and drives the downstream LM386 power amplifier input. The brief requests overall gain around 100x-200x, so this module is expected to provide a substantial portion of the voltage gain through an external feedback/bias network added later. Because only a single 9V supply is available and U1 exposes only VCC_P and VCC_N supply pins, this module must operate from VIN_9V and GND with a single-supply biasing strategy implemented by downstream passive wiring; signal interfaces must therefore preserve AC-coupled or biased handoff intent into and out of the op-amp stage. The component list provides a dual op-amp but the brief specifies one preamplifier chain feeding LM386, so one amplifier channel should implement the active preamp path while the second channel remains available for optional buffering or should be safely configured by downstream wiring without creating an additional independent signal chain.",
